---
/**
 * Founder story — Kayla and her twins. Pre-launch this doubles as the
 * site's social proof: a real parent of multiples building the thing she
 * couldn't find. Deep Teal-green background (the brand's dark surface
 * color) sets it apart from the warm/white rhythm and lets the
 * black-and-white photo carry the emotion; the blob mask on the photo ties
 * the hero's blob motif back to the two humans that inspired it.
 */
---

<section class="story section" id="story">
  <div class="container story__inner">
    <figure class="story__photo">
      <img
        src="/images/twins.jpg"
        alt="Kayla resting with her newborn twins asleep on her chest"
        width="1080"
        height="1350"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption class="story__caption">month one, hands full</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div class="story__copy">
      <p class="story__eyebrow">Why Handsful exists</p>
      <h2 class="story__title">Built by a mom who lived the blur</h2>
      <p>
        When my twins arrived, I went looking for an app to help us keep up — and there
        wasn't one. I downloaded the best singleton tracker I could find and spent months
        fighting it: switching profiles for every feed, double-logging at 3am, never quite
        sure what I'd saved for whom. It was never what I needed.
      </p>
      <p>
        That first season was a blur. No sleep, no mental clarity, leaning on my community
        for everything. An app can't hold a baby — but the right one would have made the
        hard parts simpler: night feedings half-asleep, pediatrician visits where every
        question starts with "how often…", the quiet reassurance that everyone's okay.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing was designed for parents like me, caring for more than one baby at once.
        So I'm building the thing I searched for that first night home: a tracker that
        starts where families like ours do.
      </p>
      <p class="story__signature">— Kayla, mom of twins</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Dark surface per the brand palette (Teal-green); white text is 4.9:1
     on it — passes AA for the body sizes used here. */
  .story {
    background: var(--teal);
    color: #fff;
  }
  .story__inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: clamp(var(--space-8), 6vw, var(--space-16));
  }

  .story__photo {
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }
  .story__photo img {
    width: min(380px, 100%);
    /* Organic blob mask — the hero's motif, back where it came from */
    border-radius: 58% 42% 55% 45% / 45% 55% 45% 55%;
    box-shadow: 0 24px 64px rgba(34, 32, 29, 0.35);
  }
  .story__caption {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 20px;
    font-weight: 500;
    font-style: italic;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75);
  }

  .story__eyebrow {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 15px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--butter);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .story__title {
    color: #fff;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .story__copy p:not(.story__eyebrow):not(.story__signature) {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 27px;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .story__signature {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--butter);
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .story__inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    /* Photo leads on mobile — the image is the hook, the story follows */
    .story__photo {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }
    .story__photo img {
      width: min(300px, 85%);
    }
  }
</style>
